WEBVTT

00:08.630 --> 00:10.880
Morning, Kikuchi.

00:10.880 --> 00:13.630
Good morning, Tomozaki.

00:13.920 --> 00:15.500
I read <i>The Popples</i>.

00:16.790 --> 00:18.460
You did?!

00:24.080 --> 00:27.750
I didn't know it was available as an ebook.

00:27.750 --> 00:31.250
You said the book was almost
impossible to find in stores,

00:31.500 --> 00:33.250
so I thought, "Maybe..."

00:34.000 --> 00:34.580
Here.

00:35.130 --> 00:36.040
See?

00:37.550 --> 00:41.560
<b>The Popples on Raptor Isle</b>

00:39.250 --> 00:40.330
Wow...

00:46.850 --> 00:49.070
<b>Table of Contents</b>

00:49.290 --> 00:52.830
So, um, having read it...
what did you think?

00:53.170 --> 00:55.830
I thought the best part
was at the very end,

00:55.830 --> 00:59.380
where everyone used the power of
words to convey the ocean's beauty

00:59.380 --> 01:01.830
to the blind Popple.

01:02.130 --> 01:03.710
I knew it!

01:03.960 --> 01:08.000
There was something else
that stuck with me, too.

01:08.000 --> 01:09.460
Something else?

01:10.960 --> 01:12.580
The firelings.

01:17.590 --> 01:21.970
<b>Chapter 7: The Firelings</b>

02:52.020 --> 02:57.110
<b>2nd Stage: Lv. 12
 Sometimes the ancient tome in the 
first town is the key to the final dungeon</b>

02:55.500 --> 02:57.130
The Popple makes friends with everyone...

02:57.130 --> 02:58.960
The Popple makes friends with everyone...

02:58.960 --> 03:01.040
everyone but the firelings.

03:01.290 --> 03:07.040
That's right. Not everyone can be friends.

03:07.750 --> 03:11.790
<i>The Popples</i> is... kind of a grown-up story.

03:12.790 --> 03:15.290
<i>When I read that part of </i>The Popples<i>...</i>

03:20.500 --> 03:27.170
<i>it felt about as jarring as when
Kikuchi was talking about her "ideal."</i>

03:28.420 --> 03:32.920
You said you see things from
an author's perspective, right?

03:33.670 --> 03:34.750
Right.

03:34.750 --> 03:41.040
But if that's true... you should be able
to accept that these firelings exist.

03:42.740 --> 03:48.330
<b>The Popples on Raptor Isle</b>

03:43.460 --> 03:48.330
The Popple was a freak, yet it made
friends with all these other species.

03:48.330 --> 03:49.000
<i>The Popple was a freak, yet it made
friends with all these other species.</i>

03:49.000 --> 03:51.750
<i>And yes, that's ideal.</i>

03:52.420 --> 03:55.710
<i>Still, as the author Michael
Andi crafted that world,</i>

03:55.710 --> 03:57.330
<i>he included the firelings,</i>

03:58.580 --> 04:02.500
<i>who </i>couldn't<i> make friends with the others.</i>

04:04.330 --> 04:09.170
You said that you needed
to be like the Popple...

04:09.170 --> 04:12.460
but then aren't you rejecting the firelings?

04:13.460 --> 04:15.500
If you really <i>did</i> have
an author's perspective,

04:15.500 --> 04:18.960
you'd say the world could have
both the Popple <i>and</i> the firelings.

04:19.500 --> 04:22.790
Saying that you have to be like the Popple

04:22.790 --> 04:26.580
shows that you're thinking about
how you should be for <i>yourself</i>.

04:27.380 --> 04:30.130
That may be true...

04:30.460 --> 04:33.420
<i>I know I'm playing with fire.</i>

04:33.960 --> 04:37.750
<i>I'm negating the words Kikuchi's
been using to define herself</i>

04:37.750 --> 04:40.380
<i>and trying to suggest
different words instead.</i>

04:40.960 --> 04:46.960
<i>But I see a Kikuchi who'd ushered
Kris to such a sad conclusion,</i>

04:46.960 --> 04:52.080
<i>a Kikuchi who was doing
everything she could to fit in,</i>

04:52.540 --> 04:53.920
<i>and I think, "I want to help her."</i>

04:53.920 --> 04:56.130
<i>Not that I </i>should<i> help her...</i>

04:56.880 --> 04:58.460
<i>I </i>want<i> to.</i>

04:59.880 --> 05:02.580
I don't think you need a player's
<i>or</i> an author's perspective.

05:03.080 --> 05:07.830
You can see life through your own
eyes: from a character's POV.

05:08.330 --> 05:11.580
You've just lost sight of that
because you're overthinking things.

05:13.420 --> 05:15.880
I just don't know.

05:16.380 --> 05:20.000
I don't know what I'm looking
at, what my goals are...

05:22.630 --> 05:27.130
I mean... everything I see is gray.

05:31.130 --> 05:32.670
Well, that's easy.

05:34.250 --> 05:35.500
Andi's books.

05:36.170 --> 05:39.420
You love Andi's books.

05:39.670 --> 05:42.670
That's one fact that's never going to change.

05:43.880 --> 05:45.420
Is that enough?

05:45.670 --> 05:51.210
Yep. After all, Andi's books are
what showed you a world of color.

05:51.920 --> 05:56.170
Right now, you think you
have to change to fit in.

05:56.670 --> 05:59.250
But if you were a fireling,

05:59.250 --> 06:02.750
and everyone else were a different species...

06:03.040 --> 06:06.250
you could find friends
at the firelings' lake.

06:09.130 --> 06:10.130
Is this...

06:11.710 --> 06:14.710
You'll find a bunch of friends
who like the same things.

06:15.130 --> 06:19.130
Some of whom you'll want to meet in person.

06:21.040 --> 06:24.500
I mean, that place is nothing <i>but</i> firelings.

06:26.500 --> 06:29.960
You're really amazing, Tomozaki.

06:30.290 --> 06:32.960
Nah. Just sneaky, that's all.

06:33.250 --> 06:35.750
Still... are you sure?

06:36.000 --> 06:42.210
You and Hanabi changed so
splendidly, you fit in so well...

06:42.210 --> 06:44.250
and only I stay the same?

06:44.500 --> 06:45.920
Right.

06:47.670 --> 06:49.380
I'll give it to you straight:

06:49.380 --> 06:53.130
The friendships you make at
school? They're nothing special.

06:54.630 --> 06:57.880
I've changed myself over
these past six months,

06:58.330 --> 07:00.500
<i>gotten involved with all kinds of people,</i>

07:00.500 --> 07:04.290
<i>and, I think, made a lot of
what I'd consider friends.</i>

07:05.920 --> 07:09.790
But that was all about me
clicking with those people

07:10.130 --> 07:13.420
and school was just what brought us together.

07:13.920 --> 07:16.960
<i>And in these past six months,</i>

07:17.380 --> 07:20.000
<i>the encounter I'm most happy to have had</i>

07:22.880 --> 07:29.920
<i>was the day I gave a blanket denial of
this school and the normie way of life,</i>

07:29.920 --> 07:32.040
<i>and Hinami threw it back in my face.</i>

07:33.290 --> 07:36.790
<i>I did as she said, and set
out to play the game of life.</i>

07:37.420 --> 07:42.460
<i>My superficial way of thinking
was actually sour grapes,</i>

07:42.960 --> 07:44.920
<i>a sore loser not accepting defeat.</i>

07:45.830 --> 07:48.750
<i>But that's not entirely true.</i>

07:49.500 --> 07:53.380
<i>I can't say the grapes were all that sour.</i>

07:54.750 --> 07:59.580
<i>It's simply that some grapes are
sweeter or more sour than others.</i>

08:01.330 --> 08:04.750
<i>I came to know that truth.</i>

08:06.290 --> 08:10.960
You don't need to be friends
with everyone just because

08:10.960 --> 08:13.540
you think the world demands it of you.

08:14.830 --> 08:16.290
I see...

08:16.580 --> 08:19.460
So I'm fine just as I am.

08:20.130 --> 08:26.500
I'm not some freak who doesn't
belong in this world.

08:27.420 --> 08:30.210
Right. Of course not.

08:30.500 --> 08:31.330
Right...

08:33.710 --> 08:35.710
Now, getting back on track...

08:36.080 --> 08:37.330
With what?

08:38.540 --> 08:41.710
With this here. Do you
know how to use this app?

08:43.710 --> 08:47.210
Let's see... first
you make an account...

08:48.830 --> 08:51.460
<i>It's really very simple.</i>

08:53.750 --> 08:56.380
<i>If the sweet grapes are hanging out of reach,</i>

08:56.380 --> 08:58.960
<i>seek out the sweet
strawberries on the ground.</i>

08:59.420 --> 09:03.960
<i>If you don't care for sweet things,
look for tasty nuts instead.</i>

09:04.630 --> 09:08.960
<i>And if you're not even hungry,
go have fun however you want.</i>

09:10.420 --> 09:12.960
<i>That's all there is to it.</i>

09:18.000 --> 09:19.250
Tomozaki!

09:19.580 --> 09:22.880
Morning, Kikuchi. <i>You're</i> happy today.

09:22.880 --> 09:24.880
I've made up my mind.

09:25.170 --> 09:28.250
The previous draft ended with Kris leaving

09:28.250 --> 09:32.000
and making an effort to fit
in with the outside world.

09:32.750 --> 09:37.170
But now, Kris will apprentice at
a studio to become an artisan,

09:37.170 --> 09:39.130
crafting her beloved flower decorations.

09:39.380 --> 09:41.540
Hey, nice!

09:49.000 --> 09:52.330
I'm sure Kris was lonely in her garden,

09:52.330 --> 09:54.960
and she didn't know anything
about the outside world...

09:55.830 --> 10:00.040
But I figured she'd like
working with flowers.

10:00.500 --> 10:05.920
So I think she'll be happy,
having chosen that path.

10:07.170 --> 10:08.040
Cool.

10:38.790 --> 10:40.500
Hey, Kikuchi?

10:40.500 --> 10:41.380
Yes?

10:42.790 --> 10:46.380
I'd like to talk with you about
something after the festival.

10:53.670 --> 10:55.380
Howdy, Brain!

10:55.670 --> 10:57.630
Hey, Mimimi. Morning.

10:57.630 --> 11:03.380
We're pretty much set with the
play, right? The script and all?

11:03.380 --> 11:05.250
Yeah, just about.

11:05.250 --> 11:11.380
So I can ask you to start
focusing on <i>our</i> thing now?

11:11.380 --> 11:15.500
Oh, sure. I can get some
real practice in now.

11:15.500 --> 11:19.630
Excellent! We <i>are</i> a married
couple, after all.

11:19.630 --> 11:22.920
We're doing a married-couple <i>routine</i>: an <i>act</i>.

11:24.250 --> 11:27.750
Nice comeback! Keep that up, 'kay?

11:27.750 --> 11:28.710
You bet.

11:31.750 --> 11:36.500
<i>The days leading up to the festival
were packed with rehearsals and prep.</i>

11:58.070 --> 12:03.070
<b>Sekitomo High School Culture Festival Play 
My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

12:22.220 --> 12:26.050
<b>Manga Café Banchoo</b>

12:24.960 --> 12:26.040
<i>- And now, finally...</i>

12:26.880 --> 12:29.170
<i>the festival's tomorrow!</i>

12:31.060 --> 12:33.060
<b>Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki S2</b>

12:33.060 --> 12:37.060
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

12:37.060 --> 12:41.070
<b>Sewing Room 2</b>

12:41.070 --> 12:44.450
<b>Medium Goal 
Have a girlfriend before starting year 3</b>

12:41.380 --> 12:44.460
Now, have you figured it out?

12:44.460 --> 12:49.960
Do you know who you'll choose, based
on your feelings: Fuka or Mimimi?

12:50.290 --> 12:51.830
Yes. I've decided.

12:52.210 --> 12:53.630
Good.

12:55.540 --> 12:57.670
Hey, about the play's script...

12:58.170 --> 13:01.330
How much influence did you have on the story?

13:01.630 --> 13:05.630
I was just Kikuchi's sounding
board whenever she got stuck.

13:05.630 --> 13:08.460
It's almost entirely her own work.

13:08.750 --> 13:09.500
I see.

13:09.960 --> 13:11.330
Why do you ask?

13:12.040 --> 13:13.380
No reason.

13:13.380 --> 13:17.630
I was just a little curious about
the extent of your involvement.

13:18.040 --> 13:20.380
You were at our interview, after all.

13:21.040 --> 13:23.380
Anyway, today's the big day!

13:23.830 --> 13:25.250
Are you ready?

13:25.500 --> 13:27.210
You bet I am.

13:28.740 --> 13:32.740
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

13:31.630 --> 13:32.750
<i>Today's the day I say what I feel,
so I can do what I want to do.</i>

13:32.750 --> 13:36.250
<i>Today's the day I say what I feel,
so I can do what I want to do.</i>

13:36.580 --> 13:39.040
<i>I absolutely can't afford to fail.</i>

13:39.750 --> 13:43.760
<b>Manga Café Banchoo</b>

13:42.460 --> 13:43.750
Brain!

13:44.540 --> 13:46.880
Morning, Mimi... mi...

13:46.880 --> 13:50.630
Ah! I see my appearance has you captivated!

13:53.830 --> 13:57.130
Well? Well? Cute, right? Totes adorbs?

13:57.670 --> 13:59.250
Yeah, real cute.

13:59.580 --> 14:00.750
The crab, that is.

14:00.750 --> 14:02.670
The <i>crab</i>?!

14:04.580 --> 14:08.420
All right, everyone. Get
in here for a class photo!

14:08.420 --> 14:10.330
Hey, finally!

14:11.210 --> 14:12.290
Tomozaki...

14:12.960 --> 14:14.210
Where's your T-shirt?

14:14.540 --> 14:17.210
Don't worry. I'm wearing it.

14:17.750 --> 14:18.630
See?

14:19.540 --> 14:20.630
Okay, then.

14:22.540 --> 14:26.960
This looks like it's gonna be one
fun festival. For both of us.

14:26.960 --> 14:27.750
Right?

14:28.630 --> 14:33.140
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

14:45.670 --> 14:48.040
Mizusawa! Tomozaki!

14:49.330 --> 14:54.040
Hey there, Gumi... and Mako and Sayaka!

14:55.500 --> 14:58.790
We had no idea you guys
were Gumi's friends!

14:58.790 --> 15:00.380
Long time no see!

15:00.380 --> 15:02.040
Oh, y-yeah.

15:02.040 --> 15:04.290
Huh? What happened to your nose glasses?

15:05.420 --> 15:07.290
Those were a one-day-only deal!

15:07.540 --> 15:10.290
Hey, have you seen this dude's Pinsta?

15:10.290 --> 15:11.670
Here, look.

15:12.580 --> 15:14.130
He really did post it!

15:14.420 --> 15:16.790
Those look great on you, Mizusawa.

15:16.790 --> 15:18.880
Here we go again with the non-compliments!

15:19.830 --> 15:24.670
<i>Leave it to Mizusawa...
No, I can't lose my nerve!</i>

15:25.170 --> 15:29.500
Y-Yeah, and that got a
fair number of likes, too.

15:29.500 --> 15:31.080
There you are, Brain!

15:31.750 --> 15:33.420
It's almost time...

15:39.250 --> 15:40.500
Are these girls <i>compensated</i>?!

15:40.880 --> 15:42.000
Absolutely <i>not</i>!

15:42.830 --> 15:46.670
Hey, shouldn't we get in one last rehearsal?

15:46.670 --> 15:48.500
Yeah, we should.

15:48.500 --> 15:51.250
Oh, are you doing something, Tomozaki?

15:51.250 --> 15:54.880
Um, yeah. A comedy routine, actually.

15:55.250 --> 15:56.380
Comedy?

15:57.080 --> 16:00.080
There's more to you than
meets the eye, huh, Tomozaki.

16:00.080 --> 16:02.880
Now you're doing comedy with <i>this</i> cutie?

16:03.170 --> 16:03.920
Huh?!

16:04.420 --> 16:07.380
And after you were picking up
girls at our girls' school...

16:07.630 --> 16:11.880
Y-You went to a girls'
school to <i>flirt</i>, Brain?!

16:12.130 --> 16:14.290
I-I wasn't really <i>flirting</i>, per se...

16:14.540 --> 16:22.170
B-B-Brain! Since when were
you s-such a shallow guy?!

16:22.170 --> 16:24.540
N-No! Mizusawa was—

16:24.540 --> 16:26.420
You were with <i>Takahiro</i>?!

16:26.960 --> 16:29.920
Now I <i>know</i> it's the truth!

16:29.920 --> 16:33.250
All right—let's get rehearsing!

16:33.250 --> 16:34.670
Don't change the subject!

16:35.960 --> 16:38.170
Break a leg, you two!

16:45.380 --> 16:46.580
Looking for Tomozaki?

16:47.750 --> 16:50.330
He and Mimimi should be in the
multipurpose hall right about now,

16:50.330 --> 16:51.960
doing their comedy routine.

16:52.380 --> 16:55.920
Oh, um... yes, right.

16:56.580 --> 16:57.540
Fuka?

16:58.000 --> 17:01.080
I'll do my best to make
this performance a success.

17:01.880 --> 17:05.080
I know. Thank you.

17:05.080 --> 17:07.080
<b>Multipurpose Hall 
Entrance This Way</b>

17:07.080 --> 17:09.090
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

17:11.380 --> 17:13.580
Well, th-this is it...

17:13.880 --> 17:15.830
Why are you so nervous?

17:15.830 --> 17:18.960
Sh-Shouldn't I be?

17:20.000 --> 17:24.750
Oh, it'll be fine! No one's
expecting too much, anyway.

17:24.750 --> 17:27.750
It's not like we're going to be <i>good</i>.

17:28.000 --> 17:30.500
<i>Sh-Shouldn't</i> we be?!

17:30.500 --> 17:34.500
Yes, that—right there!
Nice and natural!

17:34.960 --> 17:36.500
See? We'll be fine.

17:38.910 --> 17:44.540
<b>Comedy 
Haniwanya</b>

17:39.670 --> 17:43.170
Next up is a comedy routine from Haniwanya!

17:43.170 --> 17:44.540
All right, give it your best shot!

17:44.540 --> 17:46.170
All right, give it your best shot!

17:46.170 --> 17:48.040
<i>That's</i> our name?

17:48.290 --> 17:53.040
You don't like it? I was torn
between that and "Haniwaniwa."

17:53.040 --> 17:55.540
They're both essentially the same!

17:58.380 --> 18:00.250
Okay, Brain. Let's do this!

18:00.250 --> 18:00.960
Yeah!

18:01.550 --> 18:03.060
<b>Sekitomo Festival 
Comedy 
Haniwanya</b>

18:01.920 --> 18:03.040
Hi there!

18:03.040 --> 18:06.170
All right, here we go:

18:06.170 --> 18:08.540
Just listen to this, Tomozaki!

18:08.540 --> 18:10.290
What is it, Nanami?

18:10.290 --> 18:15.380
We've been doing this
for years and years now.

18:15.380 --> 18:18.330
We started this duo barely a month ago.

18:19.710 --> 18:22.880
Heck, we only started talking to
each other a little while back.

18:22.880 --> 18:25.330
Oh, don't say that!

18:29.580 --> 18:30.710
So anyway—

18:33.040 --> 18:33.960
Huh?

18:42.420 --> 18:45.630
<i>What's my next line again?</i>

18:47.830 --> 18:48.670
<i>Um...</i>

18:50.080 --> 18:52.290
<i>I-I have to...</i>

18:54.380 --> 18:57.250
<i>I have to... to say </i>something<i>...</i>

18:58.920 --> 19:00.130
Tomozaki!

19:00.880 --> 19:03.790
Do you know how we got our name?

19:03.790 --> 19:05.420
Um...

19:05.420 --> 19:10.080
Because you and I both love haniwa!

19:10.080 --> 19:12.210
Haniwanya!

19:12.830 --> 19:16.340
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

19:17.630 --> 19:22.830
<i>She'd go that far to cover for
me and my forgotten line...</i>

19:23.380 --> 19:24.830
<i>I've got to do something...!</i>

19:26.330 --> 19:29.460
So anyway, here we are doing comedy.

19:29.460 --> 19:30.750
Are you ignoring me?!

19:38.740 --> 19:44.740
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

19:39.040 --> 19:43.080
But listen, Nanami: I managed
to get some time off.

19:43.080 --> 19:44.170
Uh-huh?

19:44.740 --> 19:46.740
<b>Sekitomo Festival</b>

19:47.000 --> 19:49.380
Well, that went sorta okay.

19:49.380 --> 19:50.500
Yeah.

19:51.880 --> 19:56.130
Hey, I'm sorry. I totally blanked
out there. You really saved me.

19:56.130 --> 19:59.000
No problem! All part of a wife's job.

19:59.250 --> 20:01.380
Look, we are <i>not</i> married!

20:03.000 --> 20:04.710
Next time, the ramen's on me.

20:04.710 --> 20:06.380
You got it.

20:07.080 --> 20:08.880
Thanks. I mean it.

20:09.540 --> 20:13.210
All's well that ends well, right?

20:13.210 --> 20:16.290
We did pretty good for rank
amateurs... didn't we?

20:16.580 --> 20:19.380
Probably, yeah! We were definitely good!

20:19.790 --> 20:22.330
Yeah. We definitely were. Probably.

20:25.540 --> 20:27.580
I better get going.

20:27.580 --> 20:29.830
Oh, the play?

20:30.500 --> 20:33.250
The play... with Kikuchi?

20:33.710 --> 20:34.460
Yeah.

20:35.170 --> 20:36.000
I'll be back.

20:37.540 --> 20:38.540
Of course.

20:41.250 --> 20:43.580
Listen, Mimimi... I—

20:43.580 --> 20:44.540
Tomozaki?

20:47.170 --> 20:49.500
That was fun, huh? The comedy.

20:52.420 --> 20:53.210
Yeah.

20:54.250 --> 20:57.580
I really had a lot of fun.

21:02.500 --> 21:04.960
Now get going, you.

21:06.290 --> 21:06.960
Right.

21:21.420 --> 21:22.920
Aw...

21:25.460 --> 21:27.830
It's over!

21:31.880 --> 21:33.710
It's all over...

21:41.000 --> 21:42.000
Kikuchi!

21:42.830 --> 21:44.130
Tomozaki...

21:44.130 --> 21:45.750
Any minute now.

21:48.540 --> 21:49.750
Yes.

21:57.500 --> 22:01.500
And now for Class 2-2's
original performance,

22:01.500 --> 22:04.380
"My Unfamiliar Way to Fly."
